所以他们要玩一个叫“真心话大冒险”的游戏。

343
00:16:53.870 --> 00:16:57.930
How great were our toddler actors, Vince and Evan?
我们的小演员文斯和埃文表现得有多棒？

344
00:16:58.170 --> 00:16:58.750
I know.
我知道。

345
00:16:59.090 --> 00:17:00.110
So cute.
太可爱了。

346
00:17:00.390 --> 00:17:01.110
So, so good.
真的太棒了。

347
00:17:01.270 --> 00:17:09.010
Well, you know, in this scene, Dwight is trying to get Philip to choose between a dirty old beat or a check for a million dollars.
你知道，在这一幕里，德怀特试图让菲利普在脏兮兮的甜菜和一张百万美元支票之间做选择。

348
00:17:09.730 --> 00:17:16.730
And I don't know who appeared in this scene, if it was Vince or Evan, but he was only supposed to point to the beat.
我不知道这一幕里出镜的是文斯还是埃文，但他本该只指向甜菜的。

349
00:17:16.870 --> 00:17:19.150
But he said, beat.
结果他说了“甜菜”。

350
00:17:19.590 --> 00:17:20.770
Oh, it's so cute.
噢，太可爱了。

351
00:17:20.770 --> 00:17:23.830
And Dave said he was so excited.
戴夫说他当时特别兴奋。

352
00:17:24.070 --> 00:17:24.670
I bet.
我敢肯定。

353
00:17:24.930 --> 00:17:25.770
But just everything.
但就是一切都……

354
00:17:25.770 --> 00:17:28.150
He put his little hand in his jean pocket.
他把小手插进了牛仔裤口袋里。

355
00:17:28.550 --> 00:17:29.350
It was so cute.
太可爱了。

356
00:17:29.350 --> 00:17:30.170
She was so cute.
她当时太可爱了。

357
00:17:30.650 --> 00:17:33.310
So, you know, lady, I was a producer on this season.
所以，你知道，女士，我是这一季的制片人。

358
00:17:33.970 --> 00:17:38.630
And one of the things that's really cool about that is that I have a lot of digital clutter.
这件事最酷的地方在于，我有很多数字杂物。

359
00:17:39.770 --> 00:17:43.770
And so I'm going to get out a little producer digital clutter for you.
所以我打算为你整理出一点制片人的数字杂物。

360
00:17:43.930 --> 00:17:44.370
Yay.
耶。

361
00:17:44.890 --> 00:17:47.050
So I'm not very good at saving personal emails.
我不擅长保存个人邮件。

362
00:17:47.230 --> 00:17:53.630
But when I've produced things, I keep very detailed folders for my producing work.
但当我在制作节目时，我会为我的制片工作保留非常详细的文件夹。

363
00:17:53.630 --> 00:17:54.030
OK.
好的。

364
00:17:54.310 --> 00:18:01.570
So I went into my folder and I found a document titled Shruti Things Baby Philip Can Do.
所以我打开了文件夹，发现了一个标题为“施鲁蒂（Shruti）关于菲利普宝宝能做的事”的文档。

365
00:18:02.190 --> 00:18:02.750
OK.
好的。

366
00:18:03.410 --> 00:18:06.890
So sometimes the writers would do a breakout room.
有时候编剧们会进行分组讨论。

367
00:18:07.210 --> 00:18:07.390
Yeah.
是的。

368
00:18:07.630 --> 00:18:15.610
Where they would just pick a few writers to go into a room and sit there and pitch ideas on a very specific thing.
他们会挑选几位编剧到一个房间里，坐在那儿针对某个具体的事情提出创意。

369
00:18:15.790 --> 00:18:19.450
So here are some of the things that were pitched that did not make it.
以下是一些被提出来但最终没被采纳的点子。

370
00:18:19.670 --> 00:18:23.030
The baby crushes an empty soda can in his hands.
宝宝用手捏扁了一个空汽水罐。

371
00:18:23.830 --> 00:18:26.670
Philip eats dirt from Dwight's potted plant.
菲利普吃了德怀特盆栽里的土。

372
00:18:26.870 --> 00:18:29.490
Angela says he has never eaten dirt before.
安吉拉说他以前从没吃过土。

373
00:18:29.850 --> 00:18:33.490
Dwight realizes the dirt in the plant is from Shrut FarMs.
德怀特意识到盆栽里的土来自施鲁特农场。

374
00:18:33.870 --> 00:18:34.150
Mmm.
嗯。

375
00:18:34.910 --> 00:18:36.230
This one I really liked.
这个我真的很喜欢。

376
00:18:36.630 --> 00:18:39.150
The baby keeps walking into the manager's office.
宝宝不停地走进经理办公室。

377
00:18:39.470 --> 00:18:42.070
People joke that he really wants to be manager.
大家开玩笑说他真的很想当经理。

378
00:18:42.370 --> 00:18:43.370
That's cute.
那很可爱。

379
00:18:43.570 --> 00:18:44.670
And Dwight notices.
而且德怀特注意到了。

380
00:18:45.450 --> 00:18:47.210
This one also made me chuckle.
这个也让我笑了。

381
00:18:47.210 --> 00:18:54.330
Pam's mom brings her baby Philip into the office and Jim's Philip pranks Dwight's Philip.
帕姆的妈妈把她的菲利普宝宝带到办公室，吉姆的菲利普恶作剧捉弄了德怀特的菲利普。

382
00:18:56.390 --> 00:19:01.790
And finally, Dwight has a spare mustard-colored shirt hanging on the back of his office door.
最后，德怀特的办公室门后挂着一件备用的芥末色衬衫。

383
00:19:02.050 --> 00:19:05.410
Philip pulls it down and covers himself with it like a blanket.
菲利普把它拽下来，像毯子一样盖在自己身上。

384
00:19:05.670 --> 00:19:06.790
That's cute, too.
那个也很可爱。

385
00:19:07.010 --> 00:19:07.450
I know.
我知道。

386
00:19:07.450 --> 00:19:15.270
But this was like a three-page document of all the different things that baby Philip might do to reveal that he's actually Dwight's son.
但这可是个三页长的文档，列出了菲利普宝宝可能做的各种事情，以此揭示他其实是德怀特的儿子。

387
00:19:15.470 --> 00:19:16.990
Our writers were the beSt.
我们的编剧是最棒的。

388
00:19:17.210 --> 00:19:17.650
The beSt.
最棒的。

389
00:19:17.810 --> 00:19:19.490
That's what they would also do with talking heads.
他们做“访谈”环节时也是这样。

390
00:19:19.710 --> 00:19:20.050
Yes.
是的。

391
00:19:20.050 --> 00:19:21.830
And that's how we would get candy bags.
我们就是这样拿到糖果袋的。

392
00:19:22.410 --> 00:19:24.330
Our next scene takes us to the break room.
下一场戏把我们带到了休息室。

393
00:19:24.530 --> 00:19:30.010
I absolutely love this Daryl runner in this episode where everyone wants to spend time with him.
我非常喜欢这一集中达里尔的这个桥段，每个人都想和他待在一起。

394
00:19:30.390 --> 00:19:32.510
They're really bummed he did the Irish exit.
他们对他不辞而别感到非常沮丧。

395
00:19:32.770 --> 00:19:38.430
And Aaron says, okay, listen, for the next 12 hours, we each get 90-minute segments with Daryl.
于是亚伦说，好吧，听着，接下来的12个小时里，我们每个人有90分钟的时间和达里尔相处。

396
00:19:39.090 --> 00:19:40.430
And Daryl's like, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.
达里尔说，哇，哇，哇，哇。

397
00:19:40.590 --> 00:19:41.210
Wait a minute.
等一下。

398
00:19:41.410 --> 00:19:41.630
Okay.
好吧。

399
00:19:41.910 --> 00:19:44.010
Maybe I made the mistake of sneaking out of here.
也许我不该偷偷溜走。

400
00:19:44.150 --> 00:19:44.730
That's on me.
这是我的错。

401
00:19:44.770 --> 00:19:48.890
But I'm not going to spend the rest of the day here doing stuff with you guys because you're feeling sentimental.
但我可不打算在这里陪你们耗上一整天，就因为你们现在多愁善感。

402
00:19:48.890 --> 00:19:51.650
And they're instantly like, no, you have to.
结果他们立刻就说，不行，你必须得留下。

403
00:19:52.090 --> 00:19:54.510
So Daryl said, fine, pick one thing.
所以达里尔说，行吧，挑一件事。

404
00:19:55.070 --> 00:19:57.370
One thing, and I'm going to do it with all of y'all.
就一件事，我跟你们所有人一起做。

405
00:19:57.630 --> 00:20:00.590
We don't know what that thing's going to be, but they've got to go figure it out.
我们不知道那会是什么事，但他们得去商量一下。

406
00:20:00.910 --> 00:20:03.790
Well, now we're going to check in on Andy Bernard.
好了，现在我们来看看安迪·伯纳德的情况。

407
00:20:04.430 --> 00:20:06.330
The last time we saw him,
上次见到他时，

408
00:20:06.490 --> 00:20:17.550
he was frustrated because he felt like there were certain contestants who had feel-good stories and they were getting more attention than the other people in the line.
他很沮丧，因为他觉得有些参赛者有感人的故事，所以比排队里的其他人得到了更多的关注。

409
00:20:17.550 --> 00:20:21.270
Yeah, so Andy was going to make sure he had a feel-good moment.
没错，所以安迪打算确保自己也能有一个感人的时刻。

410
00:20:21.830 --> 00:20:25.850
He's going to rejoin the line dressed as an older man.
他打算扮成一个老人重新回到队伍里。

411
00:20:25.990 --> 00:20:28.050
He has put on age makeup.
他化了老年妆。

412
00:20:28.330 --> 00:20:31.310
But Casey Dean just recognizes him immediately.
但凯西·迪恩一眼就认出了他。

413
00:20:31.750 --> 00:20:34.030
And Andy's like, no, no, no, I'm an old man.
安迪还说，不不不，我是个老人。

414
00:20:34.130 --> 00:20:35.510
She's like, yeah, yeah, yeah, I get it.
她说，行行行，我懂。

415
00:20:35.790 --> 00:20:36.230
Yeah.
是啊。

416
00:20:36.390 --> 00:20:38.630
And she's like, you are shorter than before.
然后她说，你比刚才变矮了。

417
00:20:38.630 --> 00:20:44.930
And he's like, yeah, I took my lifts out because this character is my real height, unlike Andy Bernard.
他说，对啊，我把增高垫拿出来了，因为这个角色就是我的真实身高，不像安迪·伯纳德。

418
00:20:46.750 --> 00:20:48.770
Lady, this sent me on a Google search.
天哪，这让我去谷歌搜了一下。

419
00:20:49.110 --> 00:20:54.690
I became really curious about lifts in your shoes and how those work.
我真的对鞋里的增高垫以及它们是怎么运作的感到好奇。

420
00:20:54.890 --> 00:20:56.430
Well, there's a lot in Hollywood.
嗯，好莱坞里这种事很多。

421
00:20:56.810 --> 00:21:00.510
Well, that's why I got curious about it because I've heard that.
我就是因为听说了这个才感到好奇的。

422
00:21:00.670 --> 00:21:04.070
I've heard that the male stars wear the lifts in their shoes.
我听说男明星会在鞋里放增高垫。

423
00:21:04.130 --> 00:21:05.250
If they're a little shorter.
如果他们个子稍微矮一点的话。

424
00:21:05.530 --> 00:21:05.810
Yeah.
没错。

425
00:21:05.810 --> 00:21:08.110
But I'm like, how does it work?
但我心想，那到底是怎么运作的呢？

426
00:21:08.530 --> 00:21:13.290
Well, I guess that you can wear a regular shoe and it's just like how you imagine.
我想你可以穿普通的鞋子，就像你想象的那样。

427
00:21:13.490 --> 00:21:19.150
There's like just a little wedge that you put inside the sole and then it bumps you up a little bit.
里面有个小楔形垫，塞进鞋底，就能让你稍微高一点。

428
00:21:19.410 --> 00:21:26.870
Also, you might see some of your shorter male actors in a lot of cowboy boots because they have a little bit of a heel.
另外，你可能会看到一些个子较矮的男演员穿很多牛仔靴，因为那种鞋本身就有一点跟。

429
00:21:27.210 --> 00:21:29.050
That's a natural lift, right?
那是天然的增高，对吧？

430
00:21:29.230 --> 00:21:30.990
Like just the shoe gives you a lift.
就是鞋子本身就能让你变高。

431
00:21:31.130 --> 00:21:31.270
Right.
没错。

432
00:21:31.270 --> 00:21:42.750
Well, I guess one of the problems with putting lifts in your shoes is that if you go more than, I mean, a half inch, then your heel pops out the back of your shoe.
我觉得在鞋里放增高垫的一个问题是，如果你垫超过半英寸，你的脚后跟就会从鞋子里滑出来。

433
00:21:42.930 --> 00:21:46.190
So you can actually like end up walking out of your shoes.
所以你甚至可能会走着走着鞋就掉了。

434
00:21:46.190 --> 00:21:58.390
So they invented something called elevator shoes that look like a regular shoe, but they're more like a woman's wedge, like a wedge heel.
于是他们发明了一种叫“内增高鞋”的东西，看起来像普通鞋子，但更像女式的坡跟鞋。

435
00:21:58.650 --> 00:21:59.510
Oh, I'm sorry.
哦，抱歉。

436
00:21:59.510 --> 00:22:04.210
Are you talking about a sneaker that might have a little heel built in?
你是在说那种可能自带一点鞋跟的运动鞋吗？

437
00:22:04.310 --> 00:22:05.470
No, no.
不，不。

438
00:22:05.670 --> 00:22:06.590
Not what I'm wearing.
不是我穿的这种。

439
00:22:06.590 --> 00:22:12.290
No, that is not an elevator shoe because I can see that it has an exaggerated heel.
不，那不是内增高鞋，因为我能看出它有夸张的鞋跟。

440
00:22:12.590 --> 00:22:13.750
Oh, it's sneaky.
哦，那还挺隐蔽的。

441
00:22:14.110 --> 00:22:14.490
Yes.
是的。

442
00:22:14.670 --> 00:22:15.730
The elevator shoe.
这就是内增高鞋。

443
00:22:15.850 --> 00:22:22.590
I watched a whole YouTube video on it by this guy who was reviewing the best elevator shoes.
我看了个关于它的YouTube视频，是一个人在测评最好的内增高鞋。

444
00:22:22.750 --> 00:22:23.750
He was riveting.
他讲得引人入胜。

445
00:22:23.990 --> 00:22:31.970
And yeah, it looks like a beautiful, I think it's even an Italian made leather businessman shoe.
而且看起来确实像一双漂亮的皮鞋，我觉得甚至是意大利制造的商务皮鞋。

446
00:22:33.030 --> 00:22:37.550
But on the inside, I don't know, it's like the way they designed it.
但内部设计我也不清楚，反正就是那种设计。

447
00:22:37.670 --> 00:22:41.290
It just looks like a shoe, but it makes you like two inches taller.
看起来就是双普通的鞋，但能让你高出两英寸左右。

448
00:22:41.530 --> 00:22:42.190
That's a lot.
那可不少了。

449
00:22:42.470 --> 00:22:42.830
It is.
确实。

450
00:22:43.370 --> 00:22:45.650
I would be like 5'3".
那我就能有5英尺3英寸了。

451
00:22:45.650 --> 00:22:46.390
I don't know.
我不知道。

452
00:22:46.510 --> 00:22:48.090
Maybe you need an elevator shoe.
也许你需要一双增高鞋。

453
00:22:48.410 --> 00:22:49.450
I have questions.
我有些疑问。

454
00:22:50.170 --> 00:22:51.410
What's it like to walk in them?
穿上它们走路是什么感觉？

455
00:22:51.490 --> 00:22:52.950
Can you turn your ankle easily?
容易崴脚吗？

456
00:22:53.210 --> 00:22:54.610
No, it's easy to walk.
不，走起路来很轻松。

457
00:22:54.730 --> 00:23:01.110
According to the video, they're really comfortable and easy to walk in and actually better than putting a lift in your shoe.
根据视频显示，它们非常舒适，走起路来很轻松，实际上比在鞋里放增高垫要好。

458
00:23:01.110 --> 00:23:03.310
Because this forms around your foot.
因为它们能贴合你的脚型。

459
00:23:03.710 --> 00:23:08.770
The lift, this guy was saying, is actually kind of dangerous because you can walk out of your shoe.
那个人说，增高垫其实有点危险，因为你可能会从鞋子里滑出来。

460
00:23:08.910 --> 00:23:09.790
You can twist your ankle.
你可能会扭伤脚踝。

461
00:23:09.990 --> 00:23:11.910
You're not actually getting good arch support.
而且你实际上并没有得到良好的足弓支撑。

462
00:23:12.530 --> 00:23:18.970
So gentlemen out there, if you're looking for a lift, I guess the elevator shoe is what you should look into.
所以各位男士，如果你想增高，我想增高鞋才是你应该考虑的选择。

463
00:23:19.190 --> 00:23:19.690
It's your way to go.
这是你的不二之选。

464
00:23:20.270 --> 00:23:26.830
Now, the lift, obviously, you can put in and out of different pairs of shoes, which I guess gives you variety.
当然，增高垫的好处是你可以把它放进不同的鞋子里，我想这能让你有更多选择。

465
00:23:27.150 --> 00:23:28.730
But I don't know.
但我不知道。

466
00:23:28.730 --> 00:23:31.750
Well, Andy Bernard probably would love an elevator shoe.
嗯，安迪·伯纳德大概会喜欢增高鞋。

467
00:23:32.430 --> 00:23:33.550
I think he would.
我想他会喜欢的。

468
00:23:34.010 --> 00:23:35.730
But not for this character.
但这个角色不行。

469
00:23:35.910 --> 00:23:36.770
Not for old man.
老人角色不行。

470
00:23:37.030 --> 00:23:37.690
No, not for old man.
不，老人角色不行。

471
00:23:37.830 --> 00:23:38.830
Old man is shorter.
老人个子比较矮。

472
00:23:39.530 --> 00:23:45.070
Well, you know, Andy dressing up as an old man isn't going to help him because someone that works for the show comes out and says, you know what?
嗯，你知道，安迪扮成老人也没用，因为有个剧组工作人员出来说，你知道吗？

473
00:23:45.170 --> 00:23:46.410
We're done taking auditions.
我们面试结束了。

474
00:23:46.930 --> 00:23:49.270
They need everyone in the line to go home.
他们要求排队的所有人都回家。

475
00:23:49.430 --> 00:23:51.050
And Andy is furious.
安迪非常愤怒。

476
00:23:51.570 --> 00:23:52.550
He's like, no.
他心想，不行。

477
00:23:52.790 --> 00:23:55.550
And he runs past the security guard into the building.
于是他冲过保安跑进了大楼。

478
00:23:55.710 --> 00:23:56.670
Casey's going to help him out.
凯西打算帮他一把。

479
00:23:56.770 --> 00:23:57.970
She's going to form a distraction.
她准备制造点混乱。

480
00:23:58.290 --> 00:24:00.290
She jumps on the security guy's back.
她跳到了保安的背上。

481
00:24:01.270 --> 00:24:05.170
And I love her last moment where she's like, you won't be seeing the last of Casey Dean.
我特别喜欢她最后那一刻，她说，你们还会再见到凯西·迪恩的。

482
00:24:05.670 --> 00:24:06.930
We love Casey Dean.
我们爱凯西·迪恩。

483
00:24:07.070 --> 00:24:08.550
But Andy makes it inside.
但安迪还是进去了。

484
00:24:08.790 --> 00:24:09.210
He does.
他确实进去了。

485
00:24:09.210 --> 00:24:14.110
The audition moderator who gave the bad news is Ryan Bailey.
那个宣布坏消息的面试主持人是瑞安·贝利。

486
00:24:14.390 --> 00:24:17.710
He's been on Chicago Med, Arrested Development, and How I Met Your Mother.
他曾出演过《芝加哥急救》、《发展受阻》和《老爸老妈浪漫史》。

487
00:24:18.090 --> 00:24:23.670
And, you know, last week we had these great audio clips from Jessica St. Clair who played Casey Dean.
而且，你知道，上周我们收到了饰演凯西·迪恩的杰西卡·圣克莱尔发来的精彩音频片段。

488
00:24:23.670 --> 00:24:27.230
And she told us an amazing story about this scene right here.
她给我们讲了一个关于这个场景的惊人故事。

489
00:24:27.570 --> 00:24:28.510
You have to hear it.
你一定要听听。

490
00:24:28.510 --> 00:24:35.370
And something that was funny and weird was that I was, I believe, like four months pregnant.
有一件既好笑又奇怪的事，当时我大概怀孕四个月了。

491
00:24:35.770 --> 00:24:37.430
But I hadn't told anybody.
但我还没告诉任何人。

492
00:24:37.550 --> 00:24:44.930
And so I did share it with the makeup artist because I was like, sorry, my face is so puffy.
所以我告诉了化妆师，因为我说，抱歉，我的脸肿得厉害。

493
00:24:44.930 --> 00:24:46.750
And I look a little bit like the Hulk.
看起来有点像绿巨人。

494
00:24:47.510 --> 00:24:49.210
But, you know, I'm pregnant.
但你知道，我怀孕了。

495
00:24:49.210 --> 00:24:50.510
I haven't told anybody yet.
我还没告诉任何人。

496
00:24:50.650 --> 00:24:52.190
And so she's like, okay, okay.
她就说，好的，没问题。

497
00:24:52.190 --> 00:25:01.650
And there is a scene where I have to jump on the back of a security guard who's trying to, like, drag me off the set.
有一场戏是我必须跳到一个保安的背上，他当时正试图把我从片场拖走。

498
00:25:02.070 --> 00:25:09.390
And I really wanted to impress, you know, the director and, you know, and all this, one of my favorite shows.
我真的很想给导演留下深刻印象，毕竟这是我最喜欢的剧集之一。

499
00:25:09.550 --> 00:25:11.090
And so I really went crazy.
所以我真的豁出去了。

500
00:25:11.090 --> 00:25:17.330
And I, like, launched myself onto this gigantic gentleman like a cat, like a rabbit cat.
我像只猫，像只兔子猫一样，猛地扑到了那个大块头男士身上。

501
00:25:17.330 --> 00:25:26.610
And after the second take, the director ran out and he said, I don't want to step into your personal space.
拍完第二条后，导演跑出来对我说，我不想侵犯你的个人空间。

502
00:25:26.610 --> 00:25:28.590
But the makeup artist has let me know you're pregnant.
但化妆师已经告诉我你怀孕了。

503
00:25:28.770 --> 00:25:33.670
You might not want to throw yourself onto that man so violently.
你可能不想那么猛烈地扑向那个男人。

504
00:25:35.350 --> 00:25:42.810
And so I did spend a couple of takes going, God, I hope I didn't knock that baby out of me.
所以我拍那几条的时候一直在想，天哪，希望我没把孩子给撞出来。

505
00:25:42.890 --> 00:25:43.750
That would be a real shame.
那可真是太遗憾了。

506
00:25:44.510 --> 00:25:46.870
Maybe it would have been worth it for the show.
也许为了节目效果，这还是值得的。

507
00:25:48.090 --> 00:25:49.050
Oh, Jessica.
噢，杰西卡。

508
00:25:49.490 --> 00:25:50.890
She is so funny to me.
我觉得她太搞笑了。

509
00:25:50.930 --> 00:25:51.410
I know.
我知道。

510
00:25:51.690 --> 00:25:55.350
I think she's one of those people that can just read the phone book and I'd be laughing.
我觉得她属于那种就算读电话簿都能把我逗笑的人。

511
00:25:55.610 --> 00:25:55.990
I know.
我知道。

512
00:25:56.190 --> 00:25:57.190
Is that still an expression?
这还是个常用表达吗？

513
00:25:57.350 --> 00:25:58.570
People don't even say it anymore.
现在人们甚至都不这么说了。

514
00:25:58.770 --> 00:26:00.950
Because we don't really get phone books anymore.
因为我们现在基本不用电话簿了。

515
00:26:00.990 --> 00:26:03.990
Okay, insert read boring item and I'd still be laughing.
好吧，那就换成“读枯燥的东西也能把我逗笑”。

516
00:26:04.310 --> 00:26:09.950
Well, she also sent us in an audio clip just about her general takeaway from getting to do the show.
对了，她还给我们发了一段音频，讲了她参与这档节目的整体感受。

517
00:26:09.950 --> 00:26:11.150
And I want you to hear that, too.
我也想让你听听。

518
00:26:11.730 --> 00:26:14.850
So I was so excited to be with Ed in a scene.
能和艾德演对手戏我太兴奋了。

519
00:26:14.850 --> 00:26:19.670
Any time I get to be with someone from the UCB, it's very easy.
任何时候只要能和来自UCB的人合作，都会变得非常轻松。

520
00:26:19.890 --> 00:26:23.470
It's like super easy lifting because you kind of know each other's rhythMs.
就像是毫不费力的举重，因为你们了解彼此的节奏。

521
00:26:23.670 --> 00:26:28.270
And if somebody improvises, you're ready to improvise back with them.
如果有人即兴发挥，你也能随时接住戏。

522
00:26:28.750 --> 00:26:33.550
I can't remember if there were too many things that were actually improvised.
我不记得当时有没有太多即兴发挥的内容了。

523
00:26:33.770 --> 00:26:38.610
They were short little scenes, but I'm sure there were little bits and bobs back and forth.
那都是些简短的小场景，但我肯定我们之间有一些零星的互动。

524
00:26:39.270 --> 00:26:44.070
One of the things I love about Ed is he's not only wildly funny, but he's quite charming.
我喜欢艾德的一点是，他不仅极其幽默，而且非常有魅力。

525
00:26:44.170 --> 00:26:46.170
So I didn't have to act too hard.
所以我不需要太费力去演。

526
00:26:46.390 --> 00:26:49.610
You know, he's a real gentleman and a scholar.
你知道，他真是个绅士，也是个学者。

527
00:26:49.610 --> 00:26:53.830
So it was really fun to get to have like a little romantic moment with Ed.
所以能和艾德演一段浪漫的小插曲真的很有趣。

528
00:26:55.870 --> 00:26:59.810
And I remember being very panicked that I had to sing.
我记得当时非常恐慌，因为我得唱歌。

529
00:27:00.070 --> 00:27:04.410
I do that strange like, but like, I'm not a singer.
我那种感觉很奇怪，就像是，我不是个歌手。

530
00:27:04.630 --> 00:27:12.950
I mean, I'm pretty sure I was kicked out of my college acapella group, the Miss Chords,
我是说，我很确定我被大学的阿卡贝拉合唱团“Miss Chords”踢出来了，

531
00:27:12.950 --> 00:27:18.010
because instead of singing the harmony like I was supposed to, I would just sing the melody.
因为我本该唱和声，但我却只唱主旋律。

532
00:27:18.270 --> 00:27:20.610
And they finally, they were like, we're not hearing any alto.
最后他们终于说，我们根本听不到中音部。

533
00:27:20.910 --> 00:27:23.390
I'm like, and you never will, bitches, because I don't know how to do that.
我说，你们永远也听不到，你们这些碧池，因为我根本不会唱那个。

534
00:27:23.550 --> 00:27:27.170
So I remember being a little nervous about singing.
所以我记得当时对唱歌有点紧张。

535
00:27:27.430 --> 00:27:32.850
I just had to sort of go for it and hope that it wasn't too offensive to anybody's ears.
我只能豁出去了，希望这不会太刺耳。

536
00:27:34.250 --> 00:27:35.590
She's so funny.
她太搞笑了。

537
00:27:37.330 --> 00:27:40.290
Everything about that clip is so funny to me.
那段音频里的每一处都让我觉得好笑。

538
00:27:40.990 --> 00:27:45.990
If you guys want to hear more from Jessica, you have to listen to her podcast,
如果你们想听更多杰西卡的内容，一定要去听她的播客，

539
00:27:46.190 --> 00:27:48.790
The Deep Dive that she does with June, Diane, Raphael,
就是她和琼、黛安、拉斐尔一起做的《深度挖掘》，

540
00:27:48.930 --> 00:27:54.470
or download her audio book, The Art of Small Talk that she did with Casey Wilson,
或者下载她和凯西·威尔逊一起录制的有声书《闲聊的艺术》，

541
00:27:54.470 --> 00:27:56.630
because it's more of that.
因为里面全是这种内容。

542
00:27:56.770 --> 00:27:58.270
So funny.
太搞笑了。

543
00:27:59.550 --> 00:28:02.170
Well, now Dwight is going to return Philip to Angela.
现在德怀特要把菲利普还给安吉拉了。

544
00:28:02.730 --> 00:28:05.150
Oscar's going to ask Dwight if he got Philip to eat.
奥斯卡会问德怀特有没有喂菲利普吃东西。

545
00:28:05.450 --> 00:28:07.010
He said he won't take the bottle.
他说他不肯喝奶瓶。

546
00:28:07.230 --> 00:28:09.790
And Dwight says it's because he's of superior intelligence.
德怀特说那是因为他智商超群。

547
00:28:09.790 --> 00:28:12.730
He knows when he's being tricked out of a real breaSt.
他知道什么时候有人在骗他，不让他吃真奶。

548
00:28:13.350 --> 00:28:16.710
And that's when Kevin says, well, yeah, he's not that smart.
然后凯文就说，好吧，其实他没那么聪明。

549
00:28:16.930 --> 00:28:19.090
He doesn't know where I hid his toy duck.
他都不知道我把他的玩具鸭藏哪儿了。

550
00:28:19.530 --> 00:28:19.710
Yeah.
是啊。

551
00:28:20.190 --> 00:28:20.490
Kevin.
凯文。

552
00:28:20.990 --> 00:28:21.770
I know.
我知道。

553
00:28:21.990 --> 00:28:23.010
He's still jealous.
他还在嫉妒。

554
00:28:23.590 --> 00:28:25.770
Now we're going to go to Jim's desk.
现在我们要去吉姆的办公桌那边。

555
00:28:26.430 --> 00:28:29.430
There is the biggest envelope ever.
那儿有个有史以来最大的信封。

556
00:28:30.170 --> 00:28:32.250
This is a bulls**t card for me.
这对我来说是一张“胡扯”卡。

557
00:28:32.450 --> 00:28:34.070
I was going to play a bulls**t card.
我本来打算打出一张“胡扯”卡的。

558
00:28:34.070 --> 00:28:34.350
Really?
真的吗？

559
00:28:34.350 --> 00:28:35.110
Yes.
是的。

560
00:28:35.370 --> 00:28:38.370
I was going to finally play a bulls**t card here.
我本来打算终于在这里打出一张“胡扯”卡。

561
00:28:38.710 --> 00:28:44.130
You know, last week we talked about how Jim seemed to, on the fly,
你知道，上周我们讨论过吉姆似乎是如何在临时起意的情况下，

562
00:28:44.410 --> 00:28:47.390
get an idea that he needed something from the documentary crew,
想到他需要纪录片摄制组提供什么东西，

563
00:28:47.390 --> 00:28:51.610
and they immediately agree to whatever favor he needs.
而他们立刻就答应了他需要的任何帮忙。

564
00:28:51.790 --> 00:28:52.130
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

565
00:28:52.130 --> 00:28:55.710
Now I'm like, how many hours have passed,
现在我在想，到底过了多少个小时，

566
00:28:55.730 --> 00:29:00.050
and they have somehow assembled this disc for him?
他们竟然能以某种方式为他剪辑好了这张光盘？

567
00:29:00.170 --> 00:29:01.730
Nine years of footage.
九年的素材。

568
00:29:01.910 --> 00:29:02.230
I know.
我知道。

569
00:29:02.230 --> 00:29:03.270
Nine years of footage.
九年的素材。

570
00:29:03.490 --> 00:29:05.130
They edited together so quickly.
他们剪辑得太快了。

571
00:29:05.530 --> 00:29:08.070
Well, my bulls**t card wasn't so much about that.
好吧，我的“胡扯”卡指的倒不是那个。

572
00:29:08.170 --> 00:29:10.810
It was more, I titled it Big Envelope Cringe.
更多是关于——我把它命名为“大信封尴尬时刻”。

573
00:29:11.450 --> 00:29:11.910
Why?
为什么？

574
00:29:12.130 --> 00:29:14.870
Why is your bulls**t card about the size of the envelope?
为什么你的“胡扯”卡是关于信封的大小？

575
00:29:15.130 --> 00:29:17.250
Because it's, like, laughable to me.
因为这对我来说简直可笑。

576
00:29:17.390 --> 00:29:22.030
It is a giant gray envelope, and then written in huge letters,
那是一个巨大的灰色信封，上面用粗体字写着，

577
00:29:22.050 --> 00:29:24.390
it says, Jim, in Sharpie.
用记号笔写着“吉姆”。

578
00:29:24.510 --> 00:29:26.590
It's like, Cameron, did you catch the envelope?
就像是，“卡梅隆，你拍到那个信封了吗？

579
00:29:26.810 --> 00:29:27.870
Okay, let's make it bigger.
好，把它弄得更大一点。”

580
00:29:28.090 --> 00:29:31.210
It's, like, almost the size of, like, an iPad.
它几乎有iPad那么大。

581
00:29:32.010 --> 00:29:32.470
Okay.
好吧。

582
00:29:32.770 --> 00:29:35.250
The size of the envelope did not bother me in any way.
信封的大小一点儿也没困扰我。

583
00:29:35.350 --> 00:29:37.870
It felt appropriate for a disc.
我觉得对于一张光盘来说很合适。

584
00:29:38.030 --> 00:29:39.910
So we're playing two bulls**t cards.
所以我们现在要打出两张“胡扯”卡了。

585
00:29:39.910 --> 00:29:40.890
I guess so.
我想是吧。

586
00:29:41.290 --> 00:29:47.530
I mean, I just want to know how they got through all of this footage so quickly.
我是说，我只是想知道他们是怎么这么快看完所有这些素材的。

587
00:29:48.630 --> 00:29:50.350
I mean, impressive.
我是说，令人印象深刻。

588
00:29:51.010 --> 00:29:51.670
Very impressive.
非常令人印象深刻。

589
00:29:52.150 --> 00:29:55.750
Well, big envelope or not, Jim is very happy to have it.
好吧，不管信封大不大，吉姆很高兴能拿到它。

590
00:29:56.110 --> 00:29:58.550
We're going to go back to the auditions.
我们要回到试镜环节了。

591
00:29:58.590 --> 00:30:01.170
The last person is on stage.
最后一个人在舞台上。

592
00:30:01.350 --> 00:30:02.330
It's a young woman.
那是一位年轻女性。

593
00:30:02.510 --> 00:30:04.150
Yes, she's very talented.
是的，她非常有才华。

594
00:30:04.410 --> 00:30:06.750
She's singing Beautiful by Christina Aguilera,
她正在唱克里斯蒂娜·阿奎莱拉的《Beautiful》，

595
00:30:06.750 --> 00:30:08.490
and it's going very well for her.
而且她唱得非常好。

596
00:30:08.490 --> 00:30:11.810
So this gal who's singing, her name is Rachel Crow,
这个正在唱歌的女孩，她的名字叫瑞秋·克罗，

597
00:30:12.090 --> 00:30:19.550
and she was a contestant on the first season of The X Factor when she was 13 years old.
她在13岁时曾是《X音素》第一季的参赛选手。

598
00:30:19.690 --> 00:30:20.930
I have an audio clip.
我有一段音频剪辑。

599
00:30:20.930 --> 00:30:43.020
I mean, that's amazing.
我是说，那太棒了。

600
00:30:43.320 --> 00:30:44.860
She brought down the house.
她赢得了满堂喝彩。

601
00:30:45.280 --> 00:30:48.260
She went all the way to the quarterfinal round.
她一路打进了四分之一决赛。

602
00:30:48.620 --> 00:30:52.800
And after that, she went on to star in the TV series Schooled.
在那之后，她又去主演了电视剧《校园时代》。

603
00:30:52.900 --> 00:30:54.180
She did our show.
她上过我们的节目。

604
00:30:54.480 --> 00:30:56.540
She's done a fair amount of work in animation.
她在动画配音方面也做了不少工作。

605
00:30:56.540 --> 00:31:01.580
In fact, she's the voice of Tip in the Netflix show Home Adventures with Tip and O.
事实上，她还是网飞动画《小皮大冒险》中Tip的配音演员。

606
00:31:02.500 --> 00:31:03.540
She's phenomenal.
她太棒了。

607
00:31:03.540 --> 00:31:04.540
What a voice.
多好的嗓音啊。

608
00:31:04.920 --> 00:31:05.280
I know.
我知道。

609
00:31:05.760 --> 00:31:09.500
Well, I was going to point out one other person in this scene, and that is Clay Aiken.
对了，我本来想指出这一幕里的另一个人，那就是克莱·艾肯。

610
00:31:09.840 --> 00:31:10.260
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

611
00:31:10.380 --> 00:31:12.720
I was really rooting for him in American Idol.
我在《美国偶像》里真的很支持他。

612
00:31:12.940 --> 00:31:16.520
I will never forget his performance of Bridge Over Troubled Waters.
我永远不会忘记他演唱的《忧愁河上的金桥》。

613
00:31:16.740 --> 00:31:17.700
Oh, right.
噢，没错。

614
00:31:18.000 --> 00:31:18.840
So good.
太棒了。

615
00:31:19.000 --> 00:31:19.160
Yeah.
是啊。

616
00:31:19.300 --> 00:31:20.500
And I brought a clip of that.
我带来了一段那时的视频片段。

617
00:31:20.740 --> 00:31:22.180
I'm loving today.
我今天过得很开心。

618
00:31:53.000 --> 00:31:55.200
Oh, that still packs a punch.
噢，那依然很有感染力。

619
00:31:55.420 --> 00:31:56.840
I mean, I get chills.
我是说，我起鸡皮疙瘩了。

620
00:31:57.180 --> 00:31:58.180
It's so beautiful.
太美了。

621
00:31:59.100 --> 00:31:59.660
Wow.
哇。

622
00:32:00.460 --> 00:32:01.020
Wow.
哇。

623
00:32:01.560 --> 00:32:02.680
Well, let's see.
好吧，让我们看看。

624
00:32:03.300 --> 00:32:06.000
I've got a little location breakdown for you.
我给你们准备了一个拍摄地点的简要说明。

625
00:32:06.520 --> 00:32:08.480
We shot this on location.
我们是在外景地拍摄的。

626
00:32:09.000 --> 00:32:10.780
All of us had the day off.
我们所有人都放了一天假。

627
00:32:10.920 --> 00:32:11.920
It was two days off.
那是两天假。

628
00:32:12.140 --> 00:32:13.620
Ed filmed these scenes.
这些场景是埃德拍的。

629
00:32:13.620 --> 00:32:19.780
They were in Burbank, and we did not get to meet any of these folks on the day.
它们是在伯班克拍的，我们当天没能见到这些人。

630
00:32:20.000 --> 00:32:20.980
No, we didn't.
不，我们没见到。

631
00:32:21.100 --> 00:32:21.680
I know.
我知道。

632
00:32:22.220 --> 00:32:29.600
Well, Andy is going to try to sing for them, and it does not go well at all.
安迪打算为他们唱歌，但结果一点也不顺利。

633
00:32:29.880 --> 00:32:36.040
Yes, he enters as the old man, but it's very clear he's not really an old man.
是的，他以老人的身份登场，但很明显他并不是真的老人。

634
00:32:36.400 --> 00:32:37.600
Aaron Rodgers calls him out.
阿隆·罗杰斯当场拆穿了他。

635
00:32:37.720 --> 00:32:39.540
But he's going to go ahead and start singing.
但他还是决定开始唱歌。

636
00:32:40.020 --> 00:32:42.700
He's going to sing, You're Never Fully Dressed Without a Smile.
他要唱的是《没有微笑就不算盛装打扮》。

637
00:32:42.980 --> 00:32:43.340
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

638
00:32:43.600 --> 00:32:44.460
And you know what?
你知道吗？

639
00:32:44.580 --> 00:32:46.300
They aren't feeling it.
他们并不买账。

640
00:32:46.400 --> 00:32:47.320
They're not feeling it.
他们一点也不买账。

641
00:32:47.320 --> 00:32:52.540
So he quickly switches gears, and he starts singing the Cornell Fight Song.
于是他迅速转换策略，开始唱康奈尔大学的校歌。

642
00:32:52.940 --> 00:32:53.300
Yep.
没错。

643
00:32:53.660 --> 00:32:56.760
I was curious if that is the actual Cornell Fight Song.
我很好奇那是不是真正的康奈尔校歌。

644
00:32:56.920 --> 00:32:57.980
I assume it was.
我猜是的。

645
00:32:58.180 --> 00:33:03.320
And I found a compilation of Cornell a cappella groups singing it.
我找了一段康奈尔阿卡贝拉合唱团演唱这首歌的合集。

646
00:33:03.600 --> 00:33:04.620
Well, okay.
好吧，行。

647
00:33:14.750 --> 00:33:23.890
That's precious.
那太珍贵了。

648
00:33:24.130 --> 00:33:27.390
How perfect is it, though, that they're a cappella groups?
不过，由阿卡贝拉合唱团来唱，这不是很完美吗？

649
00:33:27.710 --> 00:33:28.890
Andy would be so proud.
安迪一定会引以为傲的。

650
00:33:29.250 --> 00:33:31.090
But the judges are not impressed.
但评委们并不买账。

651
00:33:31.350 --> 00:33:32.130
They're not.
并不是。

652
00:33:32.130 --> 00:33:34.670
And then Andy has a full meltdown.
然后安迪就彻底崩溃了。

653
00:33:34.990 --> 00:33:35.130
Yeah.
是啊。

654
00:33:35.290 --> 00:33:37.190
I can see them all trying not to laugh.
我能看出他们都在努力憋笑。

655
00:33:37.390 --> 00:33:37.830
Okay.
好吧。

656
00:33:38.090 --> 00:33:39.850
All of the judges are trying not to laugh.
所有的评委都在努力不让自己笑出来。

657
00:33:40.450 --> 00:33:40.930
Yes.
没错。

658
00:33:40.930 --> 00:33:43.250
I asked Santi Gold about this.
我问过桑蒂·戈尔这件事。

659
00:33:43.430 --> 00:33:44.770
Here's what she had to say.
她是这么说的。

660
00:33:45.070 --> 00:33:52.410
I think, for me, probably the funniest part and the hardest part to hold it together was when I said to him that he couldn't just sit there and cry.
我觉得对我来说，最搞笑也最难忍住不笑的部分，大概就是我跟他说他不能就坐在那儿哭的时候。

661
00:33:52.490 --> 00:33:55.190
And he's like, I can't so just sit here and cry.
然后他说，我不能就坐在这儿哭吗。

662
00:33:55.350 --> 00:33:57.950
And he's like, really, like, yells it.
而且他是那种，真的，是喊出来的。

663
00:33:57.950 --> 00:34:02.170
But just now watching it, I watched it and, like, I forgot the whole thing.
但刚才看的时候，我看着看着，就把整件事给忘了。

664
00:34:02.230 --> 00:34:03.170
And it's so funny.
真的太搞笑了。

665
00:34:03.490 --> 00:34:05.210
I mean, he did it differently every time.
我是说，他每次演的都不一样。

666
00:34:05.330 --> 00:34:08.370
So every time was, like, new opportunities to crack up laughing.
所以每一次都是让人笑喷的新机会。

667
00:34:08.370 --> 00:34:08.730
So.
所以。

668
00:34:09.150 --> 00:34:10.610
But I think that's part of the fun of it.
但我觉得这也是乐趣的一部分。

669
00:34:10.690 --> 00:34:12.990
To have to hold it together is also the fun of it.
必须忍住不笑也是乐趣所在。

670
00:34:13.090 --> 00:34:16.150
And to come up with, like, other things to do besides laugh.
还要想出除了笑以外的其他应对方式。

671
00:34:17.090 --> 00:34:18.210
Well, I really enjoyed it.
嗯，我真的很享受。

672
00:34:18.310 --> 00:34:23.750
I mean, it was kind of, like, everything that I thought that I wanted it to be, it was.
我是说，这基本上就是我所期待的一切，它确实做到了。

673
00:34:24.230 --> 00:34:28.750
And I remember talking to my friend who was, like, my main friend that we loved The Office together.
我记得当时跟我朋友聊天，他是我最好的朋友，我们俩都特别喜欢《办公室》。

674
00:34:29.150 --> 00:34:31.650
And I told him that I was on The Office and he didn't believe me.
我告诉他我上了《办公室》，他还不信。

675
00:34:31.690 --> 00:34:33.170
And he's like, you're kidding me, you know?
他说，你逗我呢吧？

676
00:34:33.310 --> 00:34:36.150
Because it was, like, a dream for that to be the first thing to do.
因为能把这作为第一份工作，简直就像做梦一样。

677
00:34:36.550 --> 00:34:41.670
And also, because it's so many years later now, a lot of people had no idea that I was ever even on there.
而且，因为现在已经过去这么多年了，很多人根本不知道我曾经上过那个节目。

678
00:34:41.850 --> 00:34:45.850
And, you know, The Office has had such a continually growing fan base.
而且你知道，《办公室》的粉丝群一直在不断壮大。

679
00:34:45.970 --> 00:34:49.630
It seems like it had a whole new life all over again, which is great.
它好像又焕发了第二次生命，这太棒了。

680
00:34:49.710 --> 00:34:50.330
It's, like, a legacy.
这就像是一种传承。

681
00:34:51.110 --> 00:34:55.390
And so people have discovered me on the end, on the end episodes.
所以人们是在最后的剧集里发现我的。

682
00:34:55.390 --> 00:34:56.850
And I'm like, oh, my God, are you in The Office?
然后他们就说，天哪，你演了《办公室》吗？

683
00:34:56.890 --> 00:35:00.550
It's really funny because it's so unexpected and it's such a nice surprise.
这真的很有趣，因为太出人意料了，是个非常棒的惊喜。

684
00:35:00.670 --> 00:35:04.370
So it just keeps surprising people all these years later.
所以这么多年过去了，它依然不断给人们带来惊喜。

685
00:35:06.820 --> 00:35:12.220
So, Angela, since I knew that this was Santi's first on-camera acting job,
那么，安吉拉，既然我知道这是桑蒂第一次出镜演戏，

686
00:35:12.420 --> 00:35:16.400
I just kind of asked her in general, like, how was that, like, coming onto the set?
我就顺便问了她，来到片场感觉怎么样？

687
00:35:16.600 --> 00:35:19.100
And she told a story that I think you'll enjoy.
她讲了一个我觉得你会喜欢的故事。

688
00:35:19.340 --> 00:35:20.100
Here it is.
就是这个。

689
00:35:21.620 --> 00:35:25.280
Yeah, so the day of, I remember coming there.
是啊，我记得那天去片场的时候。

690
00:35:25.380 --> 00:35:27.820
They told us to wear our own clothes because we were supposed to be playing ourselves.
他们让我们穿自己的衣服，因为我们要演自己。

691
00:35:28.000 --> 00:35:29.520
So that part was simple.
所以那部分很简单。

692
00:35:29.520 --> 00:35:33.120
And we just got, you know, just got out of hair and makeup and then went in.
我们做完妆发，就直接进去了。

693
00:35:33.220 --> 00:35:35.080
And it was just me, Clay Aiken, and Aaron Rodgers.
当时只有我、克莱·艾肯和阿隆·罗杰斯。

694
00:35:35.080 --> 00:35:38.360
And I knew who Clay Aiken was, but I did not know who Aaron Rodgers was.
我知道克莱·艾肯是谁，但我不知道阿隆·罗杰斯是谁。

695
00:35:38.540 --> 00:35:40.420
And I don't know anything about football.
而且我对橄榄球一窍不通。

696
00:35:41.440 --> 00:35:43.200
So I asked him, I said, oh, what do you do?
所以我问他，我说，哦，你是做什么的？

697
00:35:43.940 --> 00:35:45.720
And he's like, oh, I'm a football player.
他说，哦，我是个橄榄球运动员。

698
00:35:46.040 --> 00:35:47.880
And I said, what team do you play for?
我说，你效力于哪支球队？

699
00:35:48.020 --> 00:35:51.320
And he said, I believe he said the Green Bay Packers, if that's a team.
他说，如果那算是一支球队的话，我记得他说的是绿湾包装工队。

700
00:35:51.420 --> 00:35:51.980
I'm so bad.
我真是太糟糕了。

701
00:35:52.000 --> 00:35:53.180
I still don't know about football.
我对橄榄球还是不太了解。

702
00:35:54.120 --> 00:35:56.600
And then I asked him, what city was that?
然后我问他，那是哪个城市？

703
00:35:56.740 --> 00:35:57.580
And he told me.
他告诉了我。

704
00:35:57.660 --> 00:35:58.900
And for some reason, I thought he was joking.
不知为何，我以为他在开玩笑。

705
00:35:58.900 --> 00:36:01.040
And I was like, no, for real, what city is it?
我就说，不，说真的，到底是哪个城市？

706
00:36:01.040 --> 00:36:02.700
And he's like, no, that really is it.
他说，不，那真的是那个城市。

707
00:36:03.480 --> 00:36:04.900
So it's kind of a funny intro.
所以这算是一个挺有趣的开场。

708
00:36:05.040 --> 00:36:08.500
We ended up getting along really well and having a lot of fun throughout the day.
我们最终相处得非常融洽，一整天都过得很开心。

709
00:36:10.440 --> 00:36:17.580
But yeah, it was, I mean, I remember that they were changing the lines a lot, which made me feel a little bit anxious because I'm not used to that.
不过确实，我记得他们一直在改台词，这让我有点焦虑，因为我不习惯那样。

710
00:36:17.580 --> 00:36:23.340
And obviously didn't have any experience with that, with, I mean, with any of it at all.
显然我对此毫无经验，我是说，对这一切都毫无经验。

711
00:36:23.480 --> 00:36:32.520
It was also new, but like the improvisational aspect was so actually fun to be in and watch Ed Helms just master.
这对我来说也是全新的体验，但即兴发挥的部分真的很有趣，能看着艾德·赫尔姆斯（Ed Helms）驾驭自如真是太棒了。

712
00:36:32.880 --> 00:36:33.700
It was so funny.
太搞笑了。

713
00:36:34.200 --> 00:36:46.220
And yeah, it was hard not to laugh, but at the same time, it was fun to just be in it with him and just get to experience it and not fall apart.
是的，很难不笑场，但与此同时，能和他一起沉浸其中，去体验这一切而不笑场，真的很有趣。

714
00:36:47.980 --> 00:36:54.140
But we did it obviously several times and every time he did it different and every time it was like hilarious.
我们显然拍了好几次，他每次演的都不一样，而且每次都特别搞笑。

715
00:36:55.360 --> 00:37:03.120
And so I always, I don't know, I always just really have a fun time watching people who master their crafts and just being able to just be a witness of it.
所以我总是，我不知道，我总是很享受观看那些精通自己技艺的人表演，并能亲眼见证这一切。

716
00:37:03.160 --> 00:37:12.700
So I remember the experience being more like me getting to watch him and really, really enjoying that and just being a part of it at all, you know.
所以我记得那次经历更像是让我有机会观察他，我真的非常享受，能参与其中就很好，你知道的。

717
00:37:14.140 --> 00:37:21.960
Lady, I just love this runner of people asking Aaron Rodgers, what is it that you do?
女士，我太喜欢这个梗了，就是人们问阿隆·罗杰斯（Aaron Rodgers），你是做什么的？

718
00:37:22.140 --> 00:37:22.960
Oh, sub all.
哦，太棒了。

719
00:37:23.380 --> 00:37:24.580
That's so neat.
真有意思。

720
00:37:24.880 --> 00:37:26.280
Like, I don't know why.
我也不知道为什么。

721
00:37:26.280 --> 00:37:28.080
It's just very funny to me.
我觉得这特别好笑。

722
00:37:28.840 --> 00:37:31.980
Well, in my experience, he was really kind in the moment.
嗯，以我的经验来看，他在那一刻真的很亲切。

723
00:37:32.980 --> 00:37:38.320
Well, Dave Rodgers said all three of these guys were so great to work with.
戴夫·罗杰斯（Dave Rodgers）说这三个人都非常棒，合作起来很愉快。

724
00:37:38.520 --> 00:37:42.780
He remembered that Clay Aiken was really funny and had a great sense of humor.
他记得克莱·艾肯（Clay Aiken）非常风趣，很有幽默感。

725
00:37:42.780 --> 00:37:45.240
And he said he was really great at doing improv.
他说他在即兴表演方面真的很厉害。

726
00:37:46.220 --> 00:37:50.440
Dave said that Aaron Rodgers was really down to earth, super friendly.
戴夫说阿隆·罗杰斯非常脚踏实地，超级友好。

727
00:37:50.580 --> 00:37:51.880
He came in really prepared.
他来的时候准备得非常充分。

728
00:37:52.040 --> 00:37:54.380
He knew all his lines and gave great reactions.
他背熟了所有台词，反应也很棒。

729
00:37:54.380 --> 00:37:57.800
He really came off very relaxed and natural.
他表现得非常放松和自然。

730
00:37:58.280 --> 00:38:06.400
And he said that our editor, Claire Scanlon, was a huge fan of Santigold and was so bummed she couldn't be there.
他还说我们的剪辑师克莱尔·斯坎伦（Claire Scanlon）是桑蒂戈尔德（Santigold）的超级粉丝，因为不能到场感到非常遗憾。

731
00:38:06.820 --> 00:38:15.720
So Dave asked if Santigold would mind writing her a note and autographing it and giving it to Claire.
所以戴夫问桑蒂戈尔德介不介意给她写张便条并签个名，送给克莱尔。

732
00:38:16.060 --> 00:38:18.340
And Claire was over the moon.
克莱尔当时高兴坏了。

733
00:38:18.560 --> 00:38:20.940
That is so sweet of Dave and so thoughtful.
戴夫真是太贴心、太周到了。

734
00:38:21.240 --> 00:38:21.660
I know.
我知道。

735
00:38:21.660 --> 00:38:24.260
But also so nice of Santigold to be like, sure, no problem.
桑蒂戈尔德也很好，直接说，没问题。

736
00:38:24.440 --> 00:38:24.960
I know.
我知道。

737
00:38:25.220 --> 00:38:29.300
Well, I want to give a big thank you to Santigold for sending in all those audio clips.
嗯，我要非常感谢桑蒂戈尔德发来所有这些音频片段。

738
00:38:29.500 --> 00:38:31.880
You know, she has a podcast as well, Ange.
你知道，她也有一个播客，安吉（Ange）。

739
00:38:31.940 --> 00:38:33.560
It's called Noble Champions.
叫《高尚的冠军》（Noble Champions）。

740
00:38:34.160 --> 00:38:36.080
And here's how it is described.
以下是它的简介。

741
00:38:36.800 --> 00:38:43.420
Noble Champions is a modern-day salon created and hosted by the multi-platform visionary artist Santigold.
《高尚的冠军》是一个现代沙龙，由多平台远见艺术家桑蒂戈尔德创建并主持。

742
00:38:43.640 --> 00:38:48.620
In each episode, she sits down with some of today's leading artists, authors, activists,
在每一集中，她都会与当今一些领先的艺术家、作家、活动家坐下来交流，

743
00:38:48.620 --> 00:38:53.980
and progressive thinkers who stand up, stick up, and speak up for important causes.
以及那些为重要事业挺身而出、坚持立场并大声疾呼的进步思想家们。

744
00:38:54.320 --> 00:38:58.460
The first season is out now, and she's going to have new episodes premiering this fall.
第一季现已上线，今年秋天她还将推出新剧集。

745
00:38:58.620 --> 00:38:59.220
So check it out.
